@* How a PoSports meet is played — the one copy. The race page's intro card and the
   lobby both render this; the lobby used to carry its own with Q W A S E typed
   out by hand, which is exactly how a rebind leaves a tutorial teaching dead keys.
   The caller passes the labels of the keys that are actually bound. *@
<div>
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Lead))
    {
        <p>@Lead</p>
    }
    <ul>
        @foreach (var p in Players)
        {
            <li>
                @p.Who
                @foreach (var k in p.Sequence)
                {
                    <kbd>@k</kbd><text> </text>
                }
                in order to run · <kbd>@p.Jump</kbd> jumps
            </li>
        }
        <li>A wrong key restarts your cycle; a key before the gun is a false start</li>
        <li>Clip a hurdle and it costs +1.5s</li>
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>One row of keys: who they belong to ("Your keys:", "Player 1:") and their labels.</summary>
    public sealed record Keys(string Who, IReadOnlyList<string> Sequence, string Jump);

    [Parameter] public string? Lead { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<Keys> Players { get; set; } = [];
}
